 "scenes": [
  {
   "id": "intro",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "AVL trees balance by heights. Red-black trees balance more loosely, by colouring every node red or black and keeping a few rules about the colours. They rotate less, and they sit inside the C plus plus map, Java's TreeMap and the Linux scheduler. This video covers their rules and insertion."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "head"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Red-black trees, part 1"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Here are the eight stages."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "stages"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The five rules, black-height and the height bound, inserting a red node, and the three fix-up cases."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "stages[0..=3]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Then a full worked insertion sequence, a comparison with AVL trees, and an exam question."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "stages[4..=7]"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "rules",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 1: Cormen's five properties. Every node is red or black."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 1 of 8: five rules"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "stages"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "pr"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "pr[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The root is black. Every leaf is black, where the leaves are the nil pointers below the real nodes."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "pr[1..=2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "A red node has two black children: there are never two reds in a row on a path."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "pr[3]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "And every path from a node down to a nil passes the same number of black nodes."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "pr[4]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "These pictures have no colour, so each node is labelled R or B, and red nodes are drawn as rounded boxes."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "pr[5]"
      },
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "root black · no red-red · equal black counts"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "bh",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 2: the black-height of a node is the number of black nodes on any path from it down to a nil, not counting itself. Rule 5 makes this well defined."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 2 of 8: black-height"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "pr"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "bh"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "bh[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "By induction, a subtree whose root has black-height b holds at least 2 to the b, minus 1, keys."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "reveal",
       "target": "bh[1]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "bh[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Reds never come two in a row, so at least half the nodes on any root-to-leaf path are black: the root's black-height is at least h over 2."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "reveal",
       "target": "bh[2]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "bh[2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Put them together: n is at least 2 to the h over 2, minus 1, so h is at most 2 log 2 of n plus 1."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "reveal",
       "target": "bh[3]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "bh[3]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "A million keys: height at most 40. Looser than AVL's 29, but still logarithmic."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "reveal",
       "target": "bh[4]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "bh[4]"
      },
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "h ≤ 2 log₂(n + 1)"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "ins",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 3: to insert, first insert as in an ordinary BST: the new key becomes a leaf."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 3 of 8: the new node is red"
      },
